================================================================================
Runtime services, models, platform APIs, base images, and host substrate
================================================================================

OpenRouter - https://openrouter.ai
  Required for OmegaJev's Decisions API transport and available as an optional
  OmegaLLM inference lane. The separate page-image gateway may also use
  OpenRouter. This is a hosted service, not MIT-licensed StickerBook code;
  use is subject to OpenRouter's own terms and the terms applicable to models
  served through it.

ASI Cloud
  Optional sponsored OmegaLLM inference lane. StickerBook's current sponsored
  preset uses minimax/minimax-m3. This is a hosted inference service and remains
  subject to the provider's own terms.

Anthropic - https://www.anthropic.com
  Optional direct OmegaLLM inference lane for configured Claude models.
  Anthropic's API/service and hosted models remain subject to Anthropic's own
  terms.

OpenAI - https://openai.com
  Optional direct OmegaLLM inference lane. OpenAI's API/service and hosted
  models remain subject to OpenAI's own terms.

ASI:One - https://asi1.ai
  Optional direct OmegaLLM inference lane. The service and hosted models remain
  subject to the provider's own terms.

TypeSafe Jev - model typesafe/jev-1.13, served via OpenRouter.
  The typed discriminative decision model used by OmegaJev. The model/service
  is not relicensed by StickerBook's MIT License.

SWI-Prolog - https://www.swi-prolog.org
  Simplified BSD license. Used via the official `swipl:10.0.2` Docker image,
  which is the base of the Omega experiment image.

Python - https://www.python.org
  The StickerBook authority kernel and local browser bridge run on Python 3 and
  primarily use the Python standard library. Python retains its own upstream
  licensing; StickerBook's MIT License covers StickerBook-authored Python code,
  not the Python runtime itself.

nginx - https://nginx.org
  2-clause BSD license. Used via the official `nginx:1.27-alpine` Docker
  image as the isolated credential gateway in the older verified
  `jev/gateway/` deployment profile.

Linux Landlock / py-landlock
  Landlock is the Linux kernel security mechanism used by Omega's older
  filesystem-policy path; py-landlock is an upstream dependency in Omega's
  requirements. These are containment mechanisms, not StickerBook authority,
  and retain their own upstream licensing.

Browser Web Speech APIs
  StickerBook's optional child voice path uses browser-provided
  `SpeechRecognition` / `webkitSpeechRecognition` for speech-to-text and
  `SpeechSynthesisUtterance` / `window.speechSynthesis` for spoken replies.
  StickerBook does not bundle a speech-recognition or speech-synthesis engine.
  The browser, operating system, or browser-selected speech service may process
  audio/text under its own software license, privacy policy, and service terms.

Browser platform: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, SVG, DOM and Web APIs
  The child UI and public mechanical demo use browser-native web-platform
  features rather than a front-end framework. These platform APIs/standards are
  not StickerBook-authored libraries and are not relicensed by the project.

Docker / Docker Desktop
  Docker is the operator-controlled container substrate used to build and run
  the local Omega/OpenShell environment. Docker Desktop is part of the recorded
  Windows development-host setup. Neither Omega role receives the Docker socket.
  Docker software and services retain their own upstream licenses and/or terms.

Windows Subsystem for Linux 2 (WSL2) / Windows
  The normal development-host launcher enters WSL2 Ubuntu from Windows to run
  the trusted local lifecycle scripts. Windows, WSL2, and the Linux
  distribution are host-platform dependencies under their respective vendor
  and distribution terms; they are not covered by StickerBook's MIT grant.

GitHub Actions / GitHub Pages - https://github.com
  GitHub Actions is used for CI and static contract checks. GitHub Pages hosts
  the public mechanical demo. These are external hosting/build services, not
  components licensed under StickerBook's MIT License.

